{"t": 1792305402.9926414, "kind": "prompt", "text": "claude-1 asks: Goal from ops: automate steel at >=0.5 steel/s (30/min) from furnaces fed by belts/inserters, with steel delivered automatically into the depot provider chests at [-11.5,-29.5] area (depot at around x -16..-6, y -30..-22). No hand-feeding. Current base produces ~205 iron plates/min from somewhere (find it; likely near iron patch ~[78,52]) and coal 135/min (coal patch ~[40,94]). Depot has 20 electric drills, 40 stone furnaces, 100 inserters, 400 belts + 237, 40 undergrounds, 10 splitters, 100 poles, 1000 coal, 1600 iron plate, 200 steel. Please design: where to put the steel smelting column (likely at the existing iron smelting output), how the iron plates + coal get there, how many furnaces (stone furnaces: steel 16s, 5 plates each => 8 furnaces for 0.5/s), and how the steel gets to the depot (belt ~120 tiles, or put steel column near depot and belt plates there?). Give buildable coordinates/directions and split it into board tasks for claude-1, claude-2, claude-3 (claude-4/5 are near the iron/coal fields; tell me what they are running). Post the tasks on the board.\n[board]\n(board is empty)\n[crew] claude-1, claude-2, claude-3"}
